{"question_id": "06f04340", "question_type": "single-session-preference", "response": "Based on your memory, your confirmed homegrown ingredient is **cherry tomatoes** (you've already harvested some), and you've been cooking with **fresh basil and mint**. A weekend dinner built around them:\n\n**Main: Pesto Pasta** — basil blended with garlic, pine nuts, Parmesan, and olive oil, tossed with linguine, your homegrown cherry tomatoes, and grilled chicken (suggestion #3, 2023-05-23).\n\n**Starter or side: Caprese Salad** — fresh mozzarella, your juicy tomatoes, and basil leaves with olive oil and balsamic glaze (#1). For a mint-forward alternative, **Minty Fresh Salad** — mint, feta, cucumbers, cherry tomatoes, lemon juice, olive oil (#7).\n\n**Drink: Herby Lemonade** — lemonade infused with fresh basil and mint leaves (#11).\n\nIf your pepper plants are producing despite the aphids, the **Thai-Style Basil and Mint Stir-Fry** (#14) would put them to good use — though memory only confirms the cherry tomatoes as harvested so far.", "n_records": 64, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 5917, "completion_tokens": 1695, "calls": 2}, "selected": ["self|recipe_preferences", "self|cooking_habits", "self|garden_plants", "self|garden_harvest", "self|pest_problem", "self|pest_control_attempts", "self|gardening_interest", "self|pest_control_plans", "assistant|recipe_suggestion", "assistant|companion_plant_suggestion", "assistant|companion_plant_warning", "assistant|gardening_tip", "assistant|pest_control_suggestion", "assistant|pest_control_opinion"], "digest_bytes": 8000}
{"question_id": "38146c39", "question_type": "single-session-preference", "response": "Given your sugar experiments — turbinado worked well for you, and you like bolder flavors — a few ideas drawn from what's paired well before:\n\n- **Swap in turbinado sugar:** replace part of the granulated sugar (the same 1/4–1/2 substitution approach you're using for carrot cake works here). Turbinado's richer flavor pairs especially well with chocolate, and using a darker chocolate chip would push that rich, indulgent profile further.\n- **Add a pinch of flaky sea salt:** salt enhances turbinado's flavor, and it plays well against sweet cookie dough.\n- **Toast the nuts first:** nuts like pecans or hazelnuts pair well with turbinado, and toasting deepens the flavor.\n- **Bump the vanilla:** vanilla's creamy sweetness complements turbinado in cakes, so a little extra extract should help here too.\n- **Mind the technique:** mixing turbinado with other sugars rather than going 100%, and adjusting liquid slightly, keeps the texture from drying out.\n\nIf you want a starting point: 1/4 of the sugar swapped to turbinado, dark chocolate chips, toasted pecans, and flaky salt on top. (2023-05-28 memory: turbinado pairing entries, carrot cake substitution method, and baking tips.)", "n_records": 26, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 3552, "completion_tokens": 644, "calls": 2}, "selected": ["self|sugar_experimentation", "self|turbinado_sugar_opinion", "self|carrot_cake_plan", "self|frosting_plan", "self|flavor_preference", "assistant|turbinado_pairing_spices", "assistant|turbinado_pairing_citrus", "assistant|turbinado_pairing_nuts", "assistant|turbinado_pairing_coffee", "assistant|turbinado_pairing_vanilla", "assistant|turbinado_pairing_chocolate", "assistant|turbinado_pairing_dried_fruit", "assistant|turbinado_pairing_coconut", "assistant|turbinado_pairing_ginger", "assistant|turbinado_pairing_salt", "assistant|turbinado_cakes", "assistant|turbinado_cake_tips", "assistant|carrot_cake_turbinado_