{"question_id": "505af2f5", "question_type": "single-session-preference", "response": "Based on your current base recipe (almond milk, vanilla extract, and honey) and your goal to cut sugar, here are some twists worth trying:\n\n**Lower the sugar:** Swap the honey for stevia, monk fruit sweetener, or yacon syrup — you keep the sweetness without the sugar spike.\n\n**Make it creamier:** Trade almond milk for cashew milk or oat milk — both are creamier alternatives that give a more indulgent mouthfeel.\n\n**Boost the flavor:** Add cinnamon, nutmeg, or cardamom. These give you flavor complexity (and some health perks) with zero sugar.\n\n**Add an energy/nutrition boost:** Mix in collagen peptides, protein powder, or MCT oil — especially useful since you've been hitting that 3–4 pm energy dip.\n\nA good combo to start with: **cashew milk + vanilla + monk fruit sweetener + cinnamon + a scoop of collagen peptides.** It's creamy, lightly sweet, sugar-conscious, and pairs nicely with your homemade granola habit.", "n_records": 26, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 3456, "completion_tokens": 1095, "calls": 2}, "selected": ["self|sugar_reduction_goal", "self|money_saving_goal", "self|homemade_creamer", "self|granola_experimentation", "self|homemade_granola_batch", "self|granola_snacking_habit", "self|afternoon_sweet_cravings", "self|breakfast_skipping", "self|weekly_snack_prep_plan", "self|on_the_go_snack_needs", "assistant|creamer_sweetener_alternatives", "assistant|creamer_spice_additions", "assistant|creamer_milk_alternatives", "assistant|creamer_nutrition_boosters", "assistant|sunday_snack_prep_ideas", "assistant|granola_grain_options", "assistant|granola_variation_cinnamon_apple", "assistant|granola_variation_tropical", "assistant|granola_variation_cocoa_crunch", "assistant|on_the_go_snack_brands", "assistant|on_the_go_snack_ideas", "assistant|craving_hydration_tip", "assistant|craving_sleep_tip", "assistant|craving_meal_regularity_tip", "assistant|breakfast_ideas", "assistant|breakfast_nutrition_guidance"], "digest_bytes": 4187}
{"question_id": "fca70973", "question_type": "single-session-preference", "response": "Yes — since you've already been to Disneyland, Knott's Berry Farm, Six Flags Magic Mountain, and Universal Studios Hollywood this year, the natural next step is a **Halloween-season weekend**, which you've said interests you most. All four parks transform in the fall, so a revisit will feel like a new experience.\n\n**Top recommendation: Universal Studios Hollywood Halloween Horror Nights (mid-September through early November)**\nYou've already flagged interest in the VIP Experience's Gourmet Buffet and the Behind-the-Scenes Tour, so this is the best fit:\n- The VIP package (typically $250–$400+ per person) includes the Gourmet Buffet (savory meats, seafood, vegetarian options, decadent desserts), priority entry, front-of-line access to all mazes and attractions, an exclusive VIP lounge with complimentary snacks and a private bar, a private tour guide, and a commemorative photo plus a VIP gift like a limited-edition pin.\n- Add the **Behind-the-Scenes Tour** — about 1 hour, scheduled in the early evening before event opening, covering the makeup/FX department, maze design and construction, scare zone design, costumes, and backstage areas, with limited group size for an intimate experience.\n- Other add-ons: a private meet-and-greet with HHN's creators and designers, and VIP parking near the event entrance.\n- Book soon — VIP Experiences sell out quickly, especially during peak seasons. You can book online at universalstudioshollywood.com (Tickets > VIP Experiences) or by phone at (818) 622-8477. Note that cancellations or changes may incur fees.\n\n**Alternatives if you want a different park:**\n- **Knott's Scary Farm** (runs through the fall): haunted mazes, scare zones, live entertainment. Consider the Boo-fet (buffet meal, priority event entry, souvenir photo) and the Calico Saloon Halloween menu with bat wing chicken tenders and a signature Witch's Brew cocktail.\n- **Disneyland Halloween Time** (starts mid-September): Halloween parade, themed food like pumpkin beignets, mummy dogs, bat wing chicken tenders, and candy corn funnel cake, plus sit-down options like Blue Bayou's Halloween menu (including 'Mummy's Revenge' beef Wellington), Carthay Circle's five-course Halloween tasting menu, and Halloween character dining at PCH Grill.\n- **Six Flags Magic Mountain Fright Fest** (late September to early November): haunted mazes and scare zones, with the Fright Fest Feast (buffet, priority entry, souvenir photo) and the Full Throttle Sports Bar Halloween menu.\n\nIf you want thrills, unique food, and nighttime shows all in one weekend, Universal's HHN with the VIP Experience is the strongest match for your interests.", "n_records": 53, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 6447, "completion_tokens": 2476, "calls": 3}, "selected": ["self|theme_parks_recently_visited", "self|theme_park_interests", "self|halloween_event_interest", "self|universal_vip_gourmet_buffet_interest", "self|universal_behind_the_scenes_tour_interest", "assistant|disneyland_halloween_time", "assistant|knotts_scary_farm", "assistant|six_flags_fright_fest", "assistant|universal_halloween_horror_nights", "assistant|disneyland_holiday_season", "assistant|knotts_christmas_celebration", "assistant|six_flags_holiday_in_the_park", "assistant|universal_grinchmas", "assistant|disneyland_pumpkin_beignets", "assistant|disneyland_mummy_dogs", "assistant|disneyland_bat_wing_chicken_tenders", "assistant|disneyland_candy_corn_funnel_cake", "assistant|knotts_graveyard_dirt_cups", "assistant|knotts_mummy_meatball_subs", "assistant|knotts_skeleton_fingers_cookies", "assistant|knotts_blood_red_punch", "assistant|universal_flesh_eating_zombie_fingers", "assistant|universal_graveyard_cake_pops", "assistant|universal_mummy_hot_dogs", "assistant|universal_blood_of_the_vine", "assistant|six_flags_zombie_brain_cupcakes", "assistant|six_flags_mummy_dogs", "assistant|six_flags_skeleton_keys_lime_bars", "assistant|six_flags_witchs_brew", "assistant|disneyland_blue_bayou_halloween_menu", "assistant|disneyland_carthay_circle_halloween_feast", "assistant|disneyland_paradise_pier_halloween_character_dining", "assistant|knotts_boo_fet", "assistant|knotts_calico_saloon_halloween_menu", "assistant|universal_terror_tipsy_turvey_lounge", "assistant|six_flags_fright_fest_feast", "assistant|six_flags_full_throttle_halloween_menu", "assistant|universal_vip_gourmet_buffet_cost", "assistant|universal_vip_gourmet_buffet_contents", "assistant|universal_vip_perks", "assistant|universal_vip_lounge", "assistant|universal_vip_private_tour_guide", "assistant|universal_vip_photo_and_gift", "assistant|universal_vip_addon_behind_the_scenes_tour", "assistant|universal_vip_addon_meet_and_greet", "assistant|universal_vip_addon_parking", "assistant|universal_behind_the_scenes_tour_duration", "assistant|universal_behind_the_scenes_tour_highlights", "assistant|universal_behind_the_scenes_tour_group_size", "assistant|universal_vip_booking_online", "assistant|universal_vip_booking_phone", "assistant|universal_vip_booking_advice", "assistant|universal_vip_cancellation_policy"], "digest_bytes": 8154}
